WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.560
- I know that sometimes
when you're family,

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:05.040
things get heated, cause
I know I'm on The Voice,

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:06.720
okay, we get heated on The
Voice too, all the coach.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:08.240
We love each other, we're
like brothers and sisters,

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:09.073
- So.
- Yeah right.

00:00:09.073 --> 00:00:10.230
- I know, we are, we are,

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:11.110
seriously.
(Simon laughing)

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:14.340
And literally, it kind
of can bleed off stage.

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:16.240
Did y'all ever get in, like
an argument you're like,

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:17.510
you're not coming back from?

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:18.520
Did you ever do that?
(Simon laughing)

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:20.371
- Uh, every hour.
- Well, you came back.

00:00:20.371 --> 00:00:22.283
(audience laughing)
- Yeah, a lot of them.

00:00:22.283 --> 00:00:23.116
- Really?
- I mean I'm not kidding,

00:00:23.116 --> 00:00:24.390
every hour.
- A lot of them.

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:25.750
- Wait, why that much?

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:27.263
You're so great together, the chemistry--

00:00:27.263 --> 00:00:28.635
- Don't even start with me.

00:00:28.635 --> 00:00:29.727
(audience laughing)
- Wait, wait, wait.

00:00:29.727 --> 00:00:30.797
- Don't.
- It wasn't my fault.

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:31.630
- Don't.

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:32.833
- You just kept quitting.

00:00:32.833 --> 00:00:34.083
(Kelly cackling)

00:00:34.083 --> 00:00:34.916
- [Randy] Whoa, whoa.

00:00:34.916 --> 00:00:36.180
- That was on the first day.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:39.593
- Hey, I have been the only
girl in a panel and it is hard.

00:00:39.593 --> 00:00:41.150
It's hard to be the only girl.
- Tell me about, tell me--

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:42.500
- She was the only girl, that's true.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.497
- No, and they always use
you as, like the ditzy thing.

00:00:44.497 --> 00:00:47.366
- Never, never.
- Oh no, we wouldn't do that!

00:00:47.366 --> 00:00:48.199
(all bickering)

00:00:48.199 --> 00:00:50.337
- They planned, they planned
the whole live shows around--

00:00:50.337 --> 00:00:51.170
- Never, ever, ever.
- No.

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:52.724
- A deer caught in headlights!

00:00:52.724 --> 00:00:54.510
(audience laughing)
- Oh my God!

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:55.730
It seems like ya'll are really friendly.

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:57.530
But I do have the, this is my,

00:00:57.530 --> 00:00:58.760
actually one of my coolest things,

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:00.070
my connection with you Randy is,

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:02.030
you introduced me to somebody

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:04.150
that changed my life and my career.

00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:06.660
And I kind of quasi stole him from Justin.

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:09.590
But somebody here wants to say something

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:12.450
because I have been working
with my musical director,

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:15.330
Jason Halbert, since I dunno,
you put the band together.

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:18.310
And you put him in my path,
(clapping)

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:19.240
and I just wanted to give him a minute,

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:20.660
he wanted to tell you somethin'.

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:23.310
- You probably don't know
this but we met 18 years ago

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:25.450
and you were out with Destiny's Child,

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:27.150
and I was on tour, we were opening up.

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:29.280
And I just wanted a picture
with Beyonce, to be honest.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:30.113
(laughter)

00:01:30.113 --> 00:01:31.846
I knocked on the dressing room door

00:01:31.846 --> 00:01:34.310
and walked in the door, I was so nervous.

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:36.530
I hand the camera to
this dude, who was you,

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:37.363
and we talked in the hallway--
- I didn't know this story!

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:39.700
- Afterwards, you asked
me for my phone number.

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:41.020
I gave it to you.
- Yup, really?

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:41.913
(all laughing)

00:01:41.913 --> 00:01:44.633
- Cowell, stop it, stop it, stop it!

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:47.500
- And never heard from you, eight months--

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:49.879
(Paula shrieking with laughter)

00:01:49.879 --> 00:01:50.810
- [Kelly] This is my favorite!

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.160
- Eight months later out of the blue,

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:54.227
I'd just taken another job and
you call me up, and you said,

00:01:54.227 --> 00:01:55.793
"I've just finished a show
called American Idol,"

00:01:55.793 --> 00:01:57.787
and I called my wife and she's like,

00:01:57.787 --> 00:02:00.600
"Take the job," because she'd
been voting for, for Kelly.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:03.320
But you have no idea how
many cameramen, producers,

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:04.220
people behind the scenes--
- Yeah!

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:05.394
- That they've launched careers for.

00:02:05.394 --> 00:02:06.251
- Yes!
(audience cheering)

00:02:06.251 --> 00:02:09.880
Randy, you help, you help
and you mentor and you really

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:11.057
like, craft these musicians--
- So annoying.

00:02:11.057 --> 00:02:12.280
- And you set them up.

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:14.290
- It's always about
paying it forward, right?

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:16.580
And Jason, I'm so happy to see him here,

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:18.560
I'm happy to see Jessie
here, singing backs!

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:19.411
- [Kelly] Jessie!

00:02:19.411 --> 00:02:20.703
(audience clapping)
- Oh my God!

00:02:22.088 --> 00:02:24.520
- Is that Jessie singing background?

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:25.540
Hi Jessie.

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:26.373
(Kelly laughing)

00:02:26.373 --> 00:02:27.350
I got you the job.

00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:28.243
- Yeah.

00:02:28.243 --> 00:02:30.090
(all laughing)

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:30.923
- I love it!

00:02:30.923 --> 00:02:33.310
Okay, wait, what are some new
projects you're working on?

00:02:33.310 --> 00:02:35.380
- I got this company
called Unify Health Labs,

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:37.860
it's a whole health
wellness kind of company,

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:39.690
they're coming out with
vitamins in the next month.

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:40.523
- Really?
- Look at him!

00:02:40.523 --> 00:02:41.508
- Yes!
- Look at Randy!

00:02:41.508 --> 00:02:42.980
- We've been doing that--
- Amazing.

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:43.813
- I'm in.
- I still have my

00:02:43.813 --> 00:02:46.080
eyewear line that I've
been doing for like,

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:48.540
15 years now, Randy
Jackson Eyewear Collection,

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:49.440
managing--
- Can I put them on?

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:50.273
- Yeah.

00:02:50.273 --> 00:02:51.240
- They're actually very hot.
- Managing a ton of writers

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:53.570
and producers and artists and

00:02:53.570 --> 00:02:54.700
chefs.
(audience tittering)

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:55.910
- Got a--
- Really?

00:02:55.910 --> 00:02:57.724
- You look nice in those.
- Looks good.

00:02:57.724 --> 00:02:59.143
(audience cheering)
- You look good in those!

00:02:59.143 --> 00:02:59.976
- Randy's eyewear.

00:02:59.976 --> 00:03:02.200
- They're like the
glasses anyone can wear.

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:03.820
That's awesome, and also
I wanted to mention,

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:06.300
Paula, we saw each
other at the Billboards.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:08.240
You couldn't hear us 'cause
you're all out there being

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:09.521
another word I can't say on TV--

00:03:09.521 --> 00:03:11.823
(audience cheering)
But, like I was...

00:03:11.823 --> 00:03:15.280
When you fell, when you
fell, from the top thing,

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:16.957
I was like, "Who are you

00:03:16.957 --> 00:03:18.320
"to still be doing that?"
(Randy chortling)

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:21.620
Like I'm like, I wouldn't do
that now, like you killed it!

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:22.453
- She killed it!
- You made all of us...

00:03:22.453 --> 00:03:23.944
And I love it because--

00:03:23.944 --> 00:03:25.102
(Kelly drowned out by audience cheering)

00:03:25.102 --> 00:03:25.935
- Killed it!
- Thank you!

00:03:25.935 --> 00:03:27.620
- Killed it, killed it!
- Thank you!

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:29.987
- You did make all of
the artists there go,

00:03:29.987 --> 00:03:31.500
"Oh okay, that's how that's done."

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:32.409
Like that was,

00:03:32.409 --> 00:03:33.242
(Paula giggling)
it was so great!

00:03:33.242 --> 00:03:34.470
So what are you up to right now?

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:37.500
- Well, I have, I just opened
a residency in Las Vegas

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:38.554
at the Flamingo.
- Let's go!

00:03:38.554 --> 00:03:40.442
(audience cheering)
- I wanna see that!

00:03:40.442 --> 00:03:41.631
- Okay.
- Of course you can,

00:03:41.631 --> 00:03:42.607
you guys can come.
- You haven't invited me.

00:03:42.607 --> 00:03:44.820
- And you have a, hey mister!

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:46.140
You have like a thousand shows so,

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:47.840
like what are you working on,
well, give me the cliff notes,

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:50.200
what's happening right now,
I know America's Got Talent.

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:51.864
- Yeah, we're doing that.

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:54.917
If I'm being honest with
you, this does make me think,

00:03:54.917 --> 00:03:57.077
"If I had one wish, it would be

00:03:57.077 --> 00:04:00.330
"to make another show with us again."

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:01.163
- Aw.
- Let's go, man.

00:04:01.163 --> 00:04:02.408
- That would be my number one.

00:04:02.408 --> 00:04:04.541
- It would be so good!
- Let's go.

00:04:04.541 --> 00:04:05.433
- [Kelly] I dare you!

00:04:05.433 --> 00:04:07.880
- No, and I'll tell you why,
because apart from the fact

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:09.531
that we had so much fun and,

00:04:09.531 --> 00:04:12.720
and look, to credit
you, Kelly, like I said,

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:14.180
we wouldn't be here without you.

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:16.740
The fact that you are...

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:19.161
I mean, and one of the most
successful singers in the world.

00:04:19.161 --> 00:04:21.250
And I have to say
something about you, Kelly.

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:24.920
Unlike the majority
you are the same person

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:25.753
off camera--
- Absolutely.

00:04:25.753 --> 00:04:26.915
- 100%
- As you are on camera.

00:04:26.915 --> 00:04:28.243
(audience cheering drowns out Simon)

00:04:28.243 --> 00:04:31.810
You've always respected people,
and you've been very loyal

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:35.000
and you're a great friend
and I'm absolutely thrilled

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:36.580
for you, genuine, you deserve everything,

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:39.020
you've worked hard for it,
and for you, these guys,

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:41.720
even though everyone
remembers all the craziness,

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:44.030
what worked about that series was,

00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:47.910
is that Randy, like myself is an A&amp;R guy

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:49.540
but he was also a record producer.

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:52.700
Paula actually was a
brilliant spotter of talent.

00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:54.810
I was an A&amp;R guy, you
know, which meant I did it,

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:57.360
which was one of the
reasons why I think we had,

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:59.850
and, and this additional chemistry so,

00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:03.630
our legacy genuinely
were, are the artists we,

00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:05.980
you know, starting with
you, who we discovered

00:05:05.980 --> 00:05:07.910
over like this seven year period and

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:09.160
that's what I'm most proud of.
- A lot of them!

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:11.520
- I mean the show's ratings,
great, that's one thing,

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:13.588
but it's who came through the process

00:05:13.588 --> 00:05:17.340
is made it all worthwhile
and that's why genuinely

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:19.646
if I could choose who to
work with all over again,

00:05:19.646 --> 00:05:21.956
I would work with these guys again.

00:05:21.956 --> 00:05:23.706
(audience cheering)
- I love that!

